  "id": "COMPOUND:10896 - PROTEIN:6156",
  "verbalization": "Tiapride is shown to interact with G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging through its interaction with 6-phosphofructo-2-kinase/fructose-2,6-bisphosphatase 4. This enzyme is a target of 4-Methyl-5-[(2Z)-2-{[4-(4-morpholinyl)phenyl]imino}-2,5-dihydro-4-pyrimidinyl]-1,3-thiazol-2-amine, a compound that has been implicated in modulating cyclin B1 expression. The second pathway, involving Valacyclovir hydrolase, also leads to G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1, though with lower confidence scores. The integration of these pathways suggests that Tiapride may influence cyclin B1 through distinct but related mechanisms, potentially affecting cell cycle progression in a G2/mitotic-specific manner. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Tiapride and cyclin B1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
